{
  "id": "interface-echo",
  "title": "Every shipped interface family\u0027s generated echo reads its frame block and pass block back as the sentinels the host wrote",
  "binding": "Both legs boot an offscreen 256x256 world with ten pipeline rows, each running the generated echo pass of one shipped interface family\u0027s blocks: the ink simulation, visualize and finish passes (finish\u0027s block, the extent alone, is also Moth\u0027s and the SDF brick baker\u0027s, sdf.bricks), the pipeline-package canary\u0027s tint, the sdf.film-grain post-process package, the place and overlay engine packages, the SDF engine\u0027s per-view pass, sdf.world, whose world values its echo names as config fields, and the source-* conversion packages, whose block is the extent, the paper-white level the transfer pass converts relative to, and the work counter row and first detail row every counting pass\u0027s block carries, and the indirect cache\u0027s classify and trace passes, whose block is sdf.world\u0027s with the cache\u0027s epoch, frame, phase and update counts. Each echo reads every member of its frame group block and its pass block through the declarations the engine generates for it, compares each word with the sentinel pipeline.sentinels makes the host write at that word\u0027s offset, and writes pixel i of a one-row image green when member i reads back exactly and red otherwise. The positive leg captures each row\u0027s one initialization frame after a reset with sentinels on, and every pixel of every row is green on both backends. The discriminating leg reloads every row onto its perturbed echo, the same echo over the generated declarations but with its last member\u0027s first word expecting the sentinel of the word after it, so each row\u0027s last pixel is red, the all-green observation turns red, and the members before it still read back. InterfaceEchoCanaryFixtureTests holds each echo\u0027s blocks to its targets\u0027 and each echo file to the generator.",
  "bootShape": "offscreen",
  "backends": [
    "vulkan",
    "directx"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "gpu"
  ],
  "timeoutSeconds": 60,
